{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_06_memory_decisions", "label": "Decisions (ADR log)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/06-Memory/Decisions.md", "source_location": "L1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Architecture decision records, newest at bottom; records are never deleted, only superseded."}, {"id": "docs_06_memory_decisions_adr_001", "label": "ADR-001 Modular monolith with a worker", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/06-Memory/Decisions.md", "source_location": "L10", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three students, 25 weeks, one deploy target. One FastAPI service with strict module boundaries, one arq worker, one Postgres, one Redis: simple ops, heavy AI jobs never block requests, modules talk through service interfaces so a module can be split out later."}, {"id": "docs_06_memory_decisions_adr_002", "label": "ADR-002 Start clean, drop the Customer Insight Portal scaffold", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/06-Memory/Decisions.md", "source_location": "L17", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The folder held a scaffold and PRD for an unrelated customer-feedback analytics product; the vault replaces it and source documents moved to source-docs/."}, {"id": "docs_06_memory_decisions_adr_003", "label": "ADR-003 Hosted LLM API first, fine-tuned model later", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/06-Memory/Decisions.md", "source_location": "L23", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fine-tuning Gemma 3 / Qwen 3 before the product exists blocks every other feature. A provider interface from day one lets Claude run via API during build, fine-tune in Phase 9, and the better model per task win by config. Trade-off: early per-call cost and a PII scrub before API calls; thesis keeps its fine-tuning contribution."}, {"id": "docs_06_memory_decisions_adr_004", "label": "ADR-004 pgvector in Postgres, schema-level separation", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/06-Memory/Decisions.md", "source_location": "L30", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Patient and scholar data must never mix. One Postgres with pgvector, five schemas, per-module DB login roles and RLS on patient tables enforce separation in the database, not by convention, and remove a service (ChromaDB/Qdrant)."}, {"id": "docs_06_memory_decisions_adr_005", "label": "ADR-005 Consent-based patient to psychologist linking", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/06-Memory/Decisions.md", "source_location": "L37", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Spec said clinicians see anonymised data; proposal said clinicians forward and prioritise patients, which needs identity. Resolution: patient links by invite code and chooses scopes including identity; unlinked data stays pseudonymous."}, {"id": "docs_06_memory_decisions_adr_006", "label": "ADR-006 Vision runs in the browser by default", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/06-Memory/Decisions.md", "source_location": "L43", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Uploading webcam video of distressed people is a large privacy and cost burden. MediaPipe computes metrics locally and only numbers upload: privacy by default, no GPU in the live product, while consented research recordings keep a server pipeline for the model comparison."}, {"id": "docs_06_memory_decisions_adr_007", "label": "ADR-007 Behavioural markers never flag alone", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/06-Memory/Decisions.md", "source_location": "L50", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Webcam and voice markers vary with lighting, hardware, culture and neurodiversity; their link to clinical states is what the study tests, not an established fact. Markers appear only as context beside instrument scores with quality indicators: less demo wow, far more defensible to clinicians and the ethics committee."}, {"id": "docs_06_memory_decisions_adr_008", "label": "ADR-008 Desktop web only for the FYP", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/06-Memory/Decisions.md", "source_location": "L57", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Minimum width 1024 px; mobile and PWA deferred until after the FYP."}, {"id": "docs_06_memory_decisions_adr_009", "label": "ADR-009 English UI, Roman Urdu understood", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/06-Memory/Decisions.md", "source_location": "L62", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "English interface and instruments; counselor, crisis lexicon and filler detection handle Roman Urdu. Urdu-script UI with validated Urdu instruments comes after the FYP."}, {"id": "docs_06_memory_decisions_adr_010", "label": "ADR-010 Marketplace deferred", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/06-Memory/Decisions.md", "source_location": "L67", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Defence deck mentions booking, digital wallets, escrow and telehealth rooms; out of FYP scope and listed under Post-FYP in Phases."}, {"id": "docs_06_memory_decisions_adr_011", "label": "ADR-011 Name is ZehenSync AI", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/06-Memory/Decisions.md", "source_location": "L73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "NeuroLens in older documents refers to the same project; that name is retired."}, {"id": "docs_06_memory_decisions_adr_012", "label": "ADR-012 Two crisis responses, not one", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/06-Memory/Decisions.md", "source_location": "L78", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Spec described a single Hard Stop. Treating every PHQ-9 item 9 answer above zero as an emergency locks out people who need a gentler follow-up and teaches under-reporting, so a safety pathway handles moderate signals and Hard Stop handles high signals. Status: accepted, pending clinician review."}, {"id": "docs_06_memory_decisions_adr_013", "label": "ADR-013 Brand v1: lapis accent, Sync Z mark (superseded)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/06-Memory/Decisions.md", "source_location": "L84", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Calm clinical instrument brand: paper and ink neutrals, lapis #2E4A7D, IBM Plex + Source Serif, Sync Z mark; university-deck maroon excluded. Superseded by ADR-015."}, {"id": "docs_06_memory_decisions_adr_014", "label": "ADR-014 WeasyPrint for PDF instead of ReportLab", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/06-Memory/Decisions.md", "source_location": "L90", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Render exports from HTML templates so web and PDF share layout and styles."}, {"id": "docs_06_memory_decisions_adr_015", "label": "ADR-015 Brand v2: light clinical editorial, Zaal mark", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/06-Memory/Decisions.md", "source_location": "L94", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Team rejected v1: the Sync Z mark read as a menu icon, beige paper felt dull, the kit looked like a document. v2: Kufic Zaal mark with saffron nuqta, neel #26318A, saffron #E3A33B only as the nuqta, Newsreader + Schibsted Grotesk + Geist Mono; light product, dark brand moments."}, {"id": "docs_06_memory_decisions_fastapi", "label": "FastAPI service", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/06-Memory/Decisions.md", "source_location": "L14", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_06_memory_decisions_arq_worker", "label": "arq worker", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/06-Memory/Decisions.md", "source_location": "L14", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Runs heavy AI jobs so they never block requests."}, {"id": "docs_06_memory_decisions_postgres", "label": "Postgres 16", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/06-Memory/Decisions.md", "source_location": "L14", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_06_memory_decisions_redis", "label": "Redis", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/06-Memory/Decisions.md", "source_location": "L14", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_06_memory_decisions_pgvector", "label": "pgvector", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/06-Memory/Decisions.md", "source_location": "L34", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_06_memory_decisions_row_level_security", "label": "Row-Level Security on patient tables (five schemas, per-module roles)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/06-Memory/Decisions.md", "source_location": "L34", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_06_memory_decisions_llm_provider_interface", "label": "LLM provider interface", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/06-Memory/Decisions.md", "source_location": "L27", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Abstraction from day one so hosted and fine-tuned models are swappable per task by config."}, {"id": "docs_06_memory_decisions_claude_api", "label": "Claude API (hosted LLM)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/06-Memory/Decisions.md", "source_location": "L27", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_06_memory_decisions_gemma_3", "label": "Gemma 3 (fine-tune target)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/06-Memory/Decisions.md", "source_location": "L26", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_06_memory_decisions_qwen_3", "label": "Qwen 3 (fine-tune target)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/06-Memory/Decisions.md", "source_location": "L26", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_06_memory_decisions_pii_scrub", "label": "PII scrub before LLM API calls", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/06-Memory/Decisions.md", "source_location": "L28", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Required consequence of sending data to a hosted third-party LLM."}, {"id": "docs_06_memory_decisions_mediapipe_face_landmarker", "label": "MediaPipe Face Landmarker (in-browser)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/06-Memory/Decisions.md", "source_location": "L47", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_06_memory_decisions_yolo_v12", "label": "YOLO v12", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/06-Memory/Decisions.md", "source_location": "L47", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_06_memory_decisions_vit", "label": "Vision Transformer (ViT)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/06-Memory/Decisions.md", "source_location": "L47", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_06_memory_decisions_research_gpu_pipeline", "label": "Research recording GPU pipeline", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/06-Memory/Decisions.md", "source_location": "L47", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Separate-consent research recordings go to a server GPU pipeline so the YOLO v12 vs ViT model comparison survives while the live product stays GPU-free."}, {"id": "docs_06_memory_decisions_chromadb", "label": "ChromaDB (rejected)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/06-Memory/Decisions.md", "source_location": "L33", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_06_memory_decisions_qdrant", "label": "Qdrant (rejected)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/06-Memory/Decisions.md", "source_location": "L33", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_06_memory_decisions_customer_insight_portal", "label": "Customer Insight Portal scaffold (removed)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/06-Memory/Decisions.md", "source_location": "L20", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_06_memory_decisions_weasyprint", "label": "WeasyPrint", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/06-Memory/Decisions.md", "source_location": "L90", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_06_memory_decisions_reportlab", "label": "ReportLab (rejected)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/06-Memory/Decisions.md", "source_location": "L90", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_06_memory_decisions_neurolens", "label": "NeuroLens (retired project name)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/06-Memory/Decisions.md", "source_location": "L76", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_06_memory_decisions_sync_z_mark", "label": "Sync Z mark (retired logo)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/06-Memory/Decisions.md", "source_location": "L87", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_06_memory_decisions_zaal_mark", "label": 